fin-orders:ExecutionAllocationShape a sh:NodeShape;
    sh:description "An Execution Allocation is an immutable allocation fact that distributes one source Execution across one or more AllocationLine target accounts, used to express post-execution allocation, average-price allocation, and bunched-order back-allocation with quantity conservation, while detailed allocation and clearing semantics remain in post-trade-operations with a stable cross-module reference to the source Execution.";
