    sh:description "A Fill Snapshot is an immutable cumulative-quantity snapshot object carried by a fill-kind lifecycle event, used to express the last fill quantity, cumulative filled quantity, remaining (leaves) quantity, cancelled quantity, and average price so that the event—execution—cumulative-quantity—state closed loop is auditable without recomputation.";
